=WHAT THE VISION MODEL SAW IN THE TWO SCREENSHOTS:

{{ $json.choices[0].message.content }}

--- MEASURED FROM THE IMAGE FILES (facts, do not contradict) ---
Before canvas: {{ $('Inspect Images').first().json.before_dimensions ? $('Inspect Images').first().json.before_dimensions.width + 'x' + $('Inspect Images').first().json.before_dimensions.height : 'unknown' }}
After canvas:  {{ $('Inspect Images').first().json.after_dimensions ? $('Inspect Images').first().json.after_dimensions.width + 'x' + $('Inspect Images').first().json.after_dimensions.height : 'unknown' }}
Canvas changed: {{ $('Inspect Images').first().json.canvas_changed }}
File size change: {{ $('Inspect Images').first().json.size_delta_pct }}%
Files byte-identical: {{ $('Inspect Images').first().json.images_identical }}

{{ $('Inspect Images').first().json.context ? 'What the tester said: ' + $('Inspect Images').first().json.context : '' }}

Turn this into a structured explanation a developer can act on. Report only what the description
above states. If it says there is no visible difference, say so and return an empty list.

